"""Harness for SkyyCore 1.0.1 (GENERATED by tools/core_1_0_1_patch.py from test_skyycore_1.0.0.py: only the version texts; 1.0.1 = Movement 2,
the MoveSync copy from tools/skyymove.py - its logic is checked by python tools/skyymove_test.py). Build first:
python SkyyCore/build_skyycore_1.0.1.py

    python SkyyCore/test_skyycore_1.0.1.py [--dir <folder inside tools/dev/scratch/>] [--keep]

Every phase runs in a FRESH child JVM (the game's JRE, -Xverify:all, TEMP / TMP in the scratch folder; tools/harness_kit.py). The class
loaders copy the plugin layout: SkyyCore in its own URLClassLoader (parent = the server), a module jar in one whose parent is Core's
(Core's classes visible, like the engine's dependency bridge).
  PY      (this process) tools/skyybuild.py: semver / range_ok (the engine's range forms; a bare version refused), manifest(stable=,
          deps=) and that every old manifest stays byte-identical, core_manifest, key_parts / same_mod_keys (stable <-> versioned),
          link_core refuses a Core outside the range; tools/skyyui.py hub_bar_java_core (only the owner bookkeeping differs from the
          per-mod HubBar); tools/skyycfg.py core_template / CORE=True names; the jar: stable manifest (no Dependencies), the 59 kit files
          = the kit's sha256 pins, the 7 template classes.
  BUILD   (javassist) a sample module SkyyCoreT linked against the Core jar: its CfgData (emit CORE=True, test permission / item hooks),
          a second sample SkyyCoreU (HOME Skyy_SkyyCoreGroup/u), a per-mod CLASSIC kit + HubBar + MoveSync + status methods (the
          references the Core copies must match), and class Use (calls Core / Cfg / CfgText / HubBar / UiKit / MoveSync as a module
          does). Then the MODULE ASSEMBLE step: the 2-module test jar SkyyAsmTest 0.1.0 (alpha + beta, each its own package, data
          folder, Server Setup section, harness) + its module manifest; REFUSED: a module that calls another module's class, a
          duplicate module id, a module without Module.setup / shutdown, the same jar version with a changed module ("auto" bumps it),
          nested / other-case data folders, a DATA folder a SET jar owns (accepted with REPLACES; crosscheck data_fails then refuses
          the set while the replaced mod is in it).
  A       every class of the Core jar loads, links (-Xverify:all) and initialises in Core's own loader; the template copy there has
          no mod data and its CfgPub.start publishes NOTHING.
  API     EXECUTED: Core (version, bridge identity + cache, get / put / putIfAbsent / remove / call / has never throw, fn = a
          never-null SafeFn handle whose apply never throws and finds a late publisher, pkey = the profile
          contract incl. a throwing / empty / missing profile:fn:key, register / modules / say / readyLine / ready, selfCheck 7/7 + 59/59);
          KitLoader (names, bytes = the jar's, dataOf, two mods = two private copies); Cfg (a dead handle never throws; open = one handle
          per CfgData; start publishes config:def / config:fn / config:epoch; cmdSet / cmdSetConsole / cmdGet / op through the test
          permission hook; the file written; HOME override; the migration helpers prepare / files / histDir / histStamp / histSnapshot +
          histList + histBak read-back / logEnqueue + logFlush; shutdown); CfgText = the classic kit's CfgFile / CfgRows / CfgLog
          helpers on a corpus (same answers, same file bytes); HubBar = the per-mod HubBar (same registry -> same build() commands +
          events, handle / open / tabs answers) + the OWNER rule (removeAll(mod) removes only that mod's arrays still in place; def
          per owner); UiKit = the per-mod status / grid methods; MoveSync = the per-mod MoveSync (sums / speedFactor / jumpForce /
          fallMultiplier on random sources; ownsFall / releaseFall; a different move:proto only warns); Use.run() (a module linked
          against Core) works.
  ASM     the 2-module jar under a module loader: Modules.setupAll -> both modules up, two config kits (config:def:SkyyAsmAlpha /
          SkyyAsmBeta), each in its OWN data folder, a set through one changes only its own file + change log; shutdownAll; a
          module whose setup() throws stays OFF and the other still runs (the plugin never throws); it throws PART-WAY (kit started,
          a timer scheduled, an EMPTY store made, bridge keys put, another publisher's key replaced and one removed): its abort()
          runs once and its shutdown() never (fix round 2: shutdown() saves), the real data file stays byte-identical, the timer
          stops, every key it added is gone, the replaced / removed keys are back (same object), register() never ran, older keys
          and the running module's keys stay. A clean start runs register() once per module and shutdown() saves; a module whose
          register() throws is aborted and undone while the next module runs.
  ENGINE  HytaleServer's own PluginManifest.CODEC decodes Core's and the module jar's manifest.json (no unknown key; Dependencies
          Skyy:SkyyCore -> a SemverRange that accepts 1.0.0 / 1.9.9 and refuses 2.0.0 / 0.9.9; "^1.0.0" parses too).
  DEPLOY  tools/deploy_set.py: world keys from the jar manifests (stable / versioned), the dependency STOPs, the Core-FIRST STOP, and
          main --check on patched SETs (Core last = STOP, pilots without Core = STOP, Core first = pass; nothing is written)
  SMOKE   tools/smoke_test.py apply_deploy_config on a scratch config: Skyy:SkyyBank on + every versioned SkyyBank key off, the probe
          pair off once Core is in the run, a rollback switches the stable key off, --drop switches a mod off
  XC      tools/ci/crosscheck.py with Core + five negative jars: calling Core without the manifest dependency, naming the kit template,
          a Core range the set cannot meet, a Skyy jar depending on Hytale:EntityModule - each refused; the jars that declare Core
          resolve into it; a THIRD-PARTY jar (Group Other) depending on Hytale:EntityModule is "not checked" and does not fail
  AA      engine-access audit (tools/harness_kit.py run_audit) of the Core jar, the sample jar and the module jar.
Exit code 1 on any failure. Scratch: tools/dev/scratch/core10/core-test (deleted unless --keep).
"""
